Subject: [PATCH] Report injected internal tool content for Helix recall accounting

The virtual-model tool loop injects original text back into the prompt when the
model calls an internal recall tool (hc_recall / history_recall). That injected
text is the cost of recalling compressed history, but it was never reported,
so request_logs.compression_recall_tokens stayed 0 and the UI had nothing to
show even when recall actually fired.

The gateway has no tokenizer, so accumulate the injected content length (in
characters) per internal call name and publish it as a new internal_tool_stats
raw-trace part. CCR tokenizes it with the same gpt-tokenizer the compression
headers use, then writes compression_recall_tokens.

